<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Menedemus of Eretria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 345–261 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Menedemus of Eretria was a Greek philosopher who founded the Eretrian school, which continued the teaching of Phaedo of Elis and focused on ethics and logic. A citizen of Eretria, he also played a leading part in its politics and served on embassies to the Macedonian kings. He was known for his wit and dialectical skill, though none of his writings survives.</p></div>
